you said something about balance,

233
00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.853
that thing that still eludes me.

234
00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:36.720
And it's like, as a reader right there,

235
00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.160
that's when I was with you.

236
00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:40.860
'Cause I was like, oh,

237
00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:45.000
this guy has gone out and done all these superhuman things.

238
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.100
And one of the first things

239
00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:49.510
that he's gonna exposit us is that he still,

240
00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:51.440
here's something that he still hasn't figured out.

241
00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:54.370
No, it constantly eludes me.

242
00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:59.370
And I think that's something that will,

243
00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:02.860
I'll have to continue to work really,

244
00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:05.342
really hard on for the rest of my life.

245
00:11:05.342 --> 00:11:07.960
Being an alcoholic, being an addict,

246
00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:11.570
being in recovery, and knowing myself and my tendencies,

247
00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:16.570
and my attraction to extreme behavior, many of which,

248
00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.740
many of those don't serve me.

249
00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:22.877
And grappling with that,

250
00:11:22.877 --> 00:11:26.280
and how to live in the world with that,

251
00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.590
carrying that around is, it's not easy,

252
00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:32.320
and I'm not perfect at it by any stretch of the imagination.

253
00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:35.883
I'm usually very, very far from perfect.

254
00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:43.340
Being a drunk

255
00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:45.230
for a long time and watching people,

256
00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:46.800
watching other people getting sober

257
00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:49.560
and reading these sobriety narratives,

258
00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.890
I just operated on the assumption

259
00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:55.200
that once you stopped drinking,

260
00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:58.940
and once you got past this sort of garish,

261
00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:02.260
Hollywood dramatic DTs where you're sweating,

